%N A398286 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^(k+1) * (H(2*k)/k^3 + H(2*k,2)/k^2), where H(k) = A001008(k)/A002805(k) is the k-th harmonic number, and H(k,2) = A007406(k)/A007407(k) is the k-th generalized harmonic number of order 2.
%H A398286 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-02462-8">(Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer International Publishing, 2019, section 4.58, p. 313, section 5.58, p. 328, section 6.58, pp. 523-530.
%H A398286 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A398286 Equals 2*G^2 + 37*zeta(4)/64 = 2*G^2 + 37*Pi^4/5760, where G is Catalan's constant (A006752).
